            <title><![CDATA[US federal budget deficit jumps 12% in one year to nearly $2 Trillion (119 pts)]]></title>
            <link>https://finance.yahoo.com/economy/policy/article/the-us-federal-budget-deficit-for-2026-just-came-in-its-1992-trillion-191917669.html</link>
            <guid>50131440</guid>
            <pubDate>Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:22:05 GMT</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://finance.yahoo.com/economy/policy/article/the-us-federal-budget-deficit-for-2026-just-came-in-its-1992-trillion-191917669.html">https://finance.yahoo.com/economy/policy/article/the-us-federal-budget-deficit-for-2026-just-came-in-its-1992-trillion-191917669.html</a>, See on <a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50131440">Hacker News</a></p>
<div id="readability-page-1" class="page"><div id="main-content-wrapper">     <article data-testid="article-content-wrapper">     <div data-testid="article-body">        <p><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->The US federal budget deficit for 2026 officially came in Friday at $1.992 trillion, a final tabulation to close out the government's fiscal year and another reminder of Washington's spiraling reliance on red ink.<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>        <p><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->This deficit number represents about 6% of the <a href="https://www.bea.gov/data/gdp/gross-domestic-product" data-ylk="slk:US%20gross%20domestic%20product;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas;cpos:1;pos:1;source:content-canvas%20default" data-yga="{&quot;yLinkText&quot;:&quot;US gross domestic product&quot;,&quot;yLinkElement&quot;:&quot;context_link&quot;,&quot;yModuleName&quot;:&quot;content-canvas&quot;,&quot;yLinkPosition&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;yPosition&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;yTrafficOrigin&quot;:&quot;content-canvas default&quot;}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow"><u>US gross domestic product</u></a> and was a result of $5.403 trillion in total revenues for the fiscal year against total spending of $7.396 trillion.<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>                <p><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->The 2026 reading is a 12% jump from 2025's $1.775 trillion deficit.<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>        <p><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->These final numbers came <a href="https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/monthly-treasury-statement/summary-of-receipts-outlays-and-the-deficit-surplus-of-the-u-s-government" data-ylk="slk:in%20the%20Treasury%20Department's%20Monthly%20Statement;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas;cpos:2;pos:1;source:content-canvas%20default" data-yga="{&quot;yLinkText&quot;:&quot;in the Treasury Department's Monthly Statement&quot;,&quot;yLinkElement&quot;:&quot;context_link&quot;,&quot;yModuleName&quot;:&quot;content-canvas&quot;,&quot;yLinkPosition&quot;:&quot;2&quot;,&quot;yPosition&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;yTrafficOrigin&quot;:&quot;content-canvas default&quot;}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow"><u>in the Treasury Department's Monthly Statement</u></a> for September, which covers the final month in the US government's fiscal calendar.<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>        <p><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->The red ink has led to dire warnings from economists that the US now routinely runs annual deficits that were previously seen only during recessions and wars. The gross US national debt <a href="https://finance.yahoo.com/economy/article/us-national-debt-surpasses-40-trillion-201205840.html" data-ylk="slk:passed%20%2440%20trillion%20in%20August;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas;cpos:3;pos:1;_E:mb_qualified_link;ct:story;outcm:mb_qualified_link;source:content-canvas%20default" data-yga="{&quot;yLinkText&quot;:&quot;passed $40 trillion in August&quot;,&quot;yLinkElement&quot;:&quot;context_link&quot;,&quot;yModuleName&quot;:&quot;content-canvas&quot;,&quot;yLinkPosition&quot;:&quot;3&quot;,&quot;yPosition&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;yContentType&quot;:&quot;story&quot;,&quot;yActionOutcome&quot;:&quot;mb_qualified_link&quot;,&quot;yTrafficOrigin&quot;:&quot;content-canvas default&quot;}" target="_blank"><u>passed $40 trillion in August</u></a> and now sits above $40.3 trillion.<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>        <p><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->The latest <a href="https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/debt-to-the-penny/debt-to-the-penny" data-ylk="slk:%22Debt%20to%20the%20Penny%22;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas;cpos:4;pos:1;source:content-canvas%20default" data-yga="{&quot;yLinkText&quot;:&quot;\&quot;Debt to the Penny\&quot;&quot;,&quot;yLinkElement&quot;:&quot;context_link&quot;,&quot;yModuleName&quot;:&quot;content-canvas&quot;,&quot;yLinkPosition&quot;:&quot;4&quot;,&quot;yPosition&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;yTrafficOrigin&quot;:&quot;content-canvas default&quot;}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow"><u>"Debt to the Penny"</u></a> reading from the Treasury Department came this past Wednesday, putting the gross US national debt at $40,329,229,827,541.02.<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>   <figure data-testid="article-figure-image"><div> <p><a href="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/f88b883a0042b5406eaf6074621c3f57b9c6929b7f47060d9f101c0257ed1307/lightyear_networkapi/resizefit_w960%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fd29szjachogqwa.cloudfront.net%2Fimages%2F2026-10%2F137fce3e-4029-42c6-bef0-96fca7b3995e" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAAAAAP///ywAAAAAAQABAAACAUwAOw==" alt="WASHINGTON, DC - AUGUST 30: A view of a bus shelter at 13th and I St's NW where an electronic billboard and a poster display the current U.S. National debt per person and as a nation at 40 Trillion Dollars on August 30, 2026 in Washington, DC. (Photo by Jemal Countess/Getty Images for the Peter G. Peterson Foundation)" height="640" width="960"></a></p></div> <figcaption><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->A bus shelter in Washington display the US National debt in August. (Jemal Countess/Getty Images for the Peter G. Peterson Foundation)<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  <span data-svelte-h="svelte-nxhdlu">·</span> <span>Jemal Countess via Getty Images</span></figcaption> </figure>        <p><!-- HTML_TAG_START --><em>Read more:&nbsp;</em><a href="https://finance.yahoo.com/personal-finance/investing/article/how-the-soaring-federal-debt-affects-you-personally-155000383.html" data-ylk="slk:How%20the%20soaring%20federal%20debt%20affects%20you%20personally;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas;cpos:5;pos:1;_E:mb_qualified_link;ct:story;outcm:mb_qualified_link;source:content-canvas%20default" data-yga="{&quot;yLinkText&quot;:&quot;How the soaring federal debt affects you personally&quot;,&quot;yLinkElement&quot;:&quot;context_link&quot;,&quot;yModuleName&quot;:&quot;content-canvas&quot;,&quot;yLinkPosition&quot;:&quot;5&quot;,&quot;yPosition&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;yContentType&quot;:&quot;story&quot;,&quot;yActionOutcome&quot;:&quot;mb_qualified_link&quot;,&quot;yTrafficOrigin&quot;:&quot;content-canvas default&quot;}" target="_blank"><em>How the soaring federal debt affects you personally</em></a><!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>        <p><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->The independent budget hawks at the Committee for a Responsible Budget <a href="https://www.crfb.org/blogs/us-ran-2-trillion-deficit-last-year-we-estimate" data-ylk="slk:noted%20in%20a%20recent%20analysis%20that;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas;cpos:6;pos:1;source:content-canvas%20default" data-yga="{&quot;yLinkText&quot;:&quot;noted in a recent analysis that&quot;,&quot;yLinkElement&quot;:&quot;context_link&quot;,&quot;yModuleName&quot;:&quot;content-canvas&quot;,&quot;yLinkPosition&quot;:&quot;6&quot;,&quot;yPosition&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;yTrafficOrigin&quot;:&quot;content-canvas default&quot;}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow"><u>noted in a recent analysis that</u></a> "the country's future fiscal outlook is even more dismal," noting that annual deficits could reach $3.1 trillion by 2036 without a change in the fiscal trajectory.<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>            <p><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->The group noted that annual interest costs on the debt are now $1.1 trillion, a record 3.4% of GDP, making it the second-largest line item in the government's budget. Interest on the debt still costs less than <a href="https://finance.yahoo.com/economy/article/social-security-announces-36-cola-for-2027-the-highest-in-4-years-135447865.html" data-ylk="slk:Social%20Security;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas;cpos:7;pos:1;_E:mb_qualified_link;ct:story;outcm:mb_qualified_link;source:content-canvas%20default" data-yga="{&quot;yLinkText&quot;:&quot;Social Security&quot;,&quot;yLinkElement&quot;:&quot;context_link&quot;,&quot;yModuleName&quot;:&quot;content-canvas&quot;,&quot;yLinkPosition&quot;:&quot;7&quot;,&quot;yPosition&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;yContentType&quot;:&quot;story&quot;,&quot;yActionOutcome&quot;:&quot;mb_qualified_link&quot;,&quot;yTrafficOrigin&quot;:&quot;content-canvas default&quot;}" target="_blank">Social Security</a>, but it is now more expensive than either Medicare or the defense budget.<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>        <p><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->Members of President Trump's team have tried to downplay this year's tabulation — the highest annual deficit reading other than 2020 and 2021, when budgets were inflated by COVID-era spending — as a blip and insist that the US fiscal situation is getting under control.<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>        <p><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent has focused on the Supreme Court-ordered tariff refunds that have turned a revenue stream <a href="https://finance.yahoo.com/economy/article/new-data-shows-the-us-governments-166-billion-tariff-refund-process-is-quickly-tapering-off-201348435.html" data-ylk="slk:into%20a%20cost%20center%20for%20the%20government%20in%20recent%20months.;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas;cpos:8;pos:1;_E:mb_qualified_link;ct:story;outcm:mb_qualified_link;source:content-canvas%20default" data-yga="{&quot;yLinkText&quot;:&quot;into a cost center for the government in recent months.&quot;,&quot;yLinkElement&quot;:&quot;context_link&quot;,&quot;yModuleName&quot;:&quot;content-canvas&quot;,&quot;yLinkPosition&quot;:&quot;8&quot;,&quot;yPosition&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;yContentType&quot;:&quot;story&quot;,&quot;yActionOutcome&quot;:&quot;mb_qualified_link&quot;,&quot;yTrafficOrigin&quot;:&quot;content-canvas default&quot;}" target="_blank"><u>into a cost center for the government in recent months.</u></a><!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>        <p><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->Indeed, the impact of tariff refunds has been significant: $144.6 billion in tariff refunds were given out over the past year — but analyses of the deficit also show a variety of factors that have driven up deficits.<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>   <figure data-testid="article-figure-image"><div> <p><a href="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/e81695da75e610fc1f31ba54ed624fcab83cca3939c3d190fab79c5e09de882c/lightyear_networkapi/resizefit_w960%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fd29szjachogqwa.cloudfront.net%2Fimages%2F2026-10%2Fce5f3393-d53f-48ea-91b1-aac1887c024f" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAAAAAP///ywAAAAAAQABAAACAUwAOw==" alt="WASHINGTON, DC - OCTOBER 07: U.S. Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent (L) makes a statement alongside U.S. President Donald Trump  during an event in the Oval Office of the White House on October 07, 2026 in Washington, DC. President Trump announced that automatic enrollment in the $1,000 government seed deposit for children born between 2025 and 2028 known as &quot;Trump Accounts&quot; is now active. (Photo by Anna Moneymaker/Getty Images)" height="640" width="960"></a></p></div> <figcaption><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent and President Trump are seen during an event in the Oval Office of the White House on Oct. 7. (Anna Moneymaker/Getty Images)<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  <span data-svelte-h="svelte-nxhdlu">·</span> <span>Anna Moneymaker via Getty Images</span></figcaption> </figure>         <p><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->A <a href="https://www.hamiltonproject.org/data/tracking-federal-expenditures-in-real-time/" data-ylk="slk:Hamilton%20Project%20tracker%20of%20government%20expenditures;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas;cpos:9;pos:1;source:content-canvas%20default" data-yga="{&quot;yLinkText&quot;:&quot;Hamilton Project tracker of government expenditures&quot;,&quot;yLinkElement&quot;:&quot;context_link&quot;,&quot;yModuleName&quot;:&quot;content-canvas&quot;,&quot;yLinkPosition&quot;:&quot;9&quot;,&quot;yPosition&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;yTrafficOrigin&quot;:&quot;content-canvas default&quot;}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow"><u>Hamilton Project tracker of government expenditures</u></a> shows how government spending has increased at a steady pace in 2026. The tracker looks at spending by calendar year and shows that as of Oct. 14, government spending has jumped each of the last three years.<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>  </div> <span> </span> </article>      </div></div>]]></description>
        </item>
