        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[Making Chicken Transparent Using Dorito Dust (125 pts)]]></title>
            <link>https://chillphysicsenjoyer.substack.com/p/making-chicken-transparent-using</link>
            <guid>50131213</guid>
            <pubDate>Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:55:28 GMT</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://chillphysicsenjoyer.substack.com/p/making-chicken-transparent-using">https://chillphysicsenjoyer.substack.com/p/making-chicken-transparent-using</a>, See on <a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50131213">Hacker News</a></p>
<div id="readability-page-1" class="page"><div><article><div dir="auto"><p><em>Thank you </em><span data-state="closed"><a href="https://open.substack.com/users/2340896-adaobi?utm_source=mentions" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-attrs="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Adaobi&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:2340896,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:null,&quot;photo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/a83b4440-0070-44d3-a255-65a04709fe27_1179x1179.jpeg&quot;,&quot;uuid&quot;:&quot;ec2baa5b-a482-4756-bfd3-b9c0fa08d5e1&quot;}" data-component-name="MentionUser">Adaobi</a></span><span> </span><em>for such a wonderful suggestion. All credit to her for the idea, we are still workin’ on it!</em></p><p><span>My genius friend Adaobi Adibe sent me a paper on making biological tissues transparent. In </span><a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11931656/?utm_source=chatgpt.com">“Achieving optical transparency in live animals with absorbing molecules”</a><span>, the authors make biological tissues, like chicken breast, transparent by soaking them in a solution of tartrazine. Tartrazine is the very bright yellowish-orange food dye that is found on Doritos.</span></p><p>We aim to do a more ambitious replication imminently. But as a warm up, I tried to replicate parts of this protocol by soaking chicken breast in tartrazine solution. I got partial transparency but not to the degree of the paper. The sample below is an approximately 2mm thick raw chicken breast cut from a 5mm slice that was soaked in ~0.19 M tartrazine solution for 6 hours at room temperature. I took an image of this with a desk light. You can see the grid lines showing through from underneath. The chicken, even though the texture to the touch is the same, has a visual quality like that of gummy bears.</p><div><figure><a target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HeYS!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc2335aaa-1716-4bb2-94bb-7de424fec71f_1200x669.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HeYS!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc2335aaa-1716-4bb2-94bb-7de424fec71f_1200x669.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HeYS!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc2335aaa-1716-4bb2-94bb-7de424fec71f_1200x669.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HeYS!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc2335aaa-1716-4bb2-94bb-7de424fec71f_1200x669.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HeYS!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc2335aaa-1716-4bb2-94bb-7de424fec71f_1200x669.png 1456w" sizes="100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HeYS!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc2335aaa-1716-4bb2-94bb-7de424fec71f_1200x669.png" width="728" height="409.5" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/c2335aaa-1716-4bb2-94bb-7de424fec71f_1200x669.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:false,&quot;imageSize&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;height&quot;:819,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:728,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;captionedImage&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HeYS!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc2335aaa-1716-4bb2-94bb-7de424fec71f_1200x669.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HeYS!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc2335aaa-1716-4bb2-94bb-7de424fec71f_1200x669.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HeYS!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc2335aaa-1716-4bb2-94bb-7de424fec71f_1200x669.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HeYS!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc2335aaa-1716-4bb2-94bb-7de424fec71f_1200x669.png 1456w" sizes="100vw" fetchpriority="high"></picture></div></a></figure></div><p>The original paper used 0.62 M, 40 °C and a machine shaker, but I couldn't find a way to do this safely, nor did I have the equipment to do so. Hence the altered protocol.</p><p>The image below is a different angle of my sample. The sample on the left is the same 2mm thick chicken breast slice as above. And the sample on the right is a control where I soaked it in water (it is slightly yellow since this process is super messy and I got dust on it).</p><div><figure><a target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mZ-P!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd8f6dad4-eb94-4b40-bfac-bdc9f21b3cff_639x794.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mZ-P!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd8f6dad4-eb94-4b40-bfac-bdc9f21b3cff_639x794.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mZ-P!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd8f6dad4-eb94-4b40-bfac-bdc9f21b3cff_639x794.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mZ-P!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd8f6dad4-eb94-4b40-bfac-bdc9f21b3cff_639x794.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mZ-P!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd8f6dad4-eb94-4b40-bfac-bdc9f21b3cff_639x794.png 1456w" sizes="100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mZ-P!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd8f6dad4-eb94-4b40-bfac-bdc9f21b3cff_639x794.png" width="728" height="409.5" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/d8f6dad4-eb94-4b40-bfac-bdc9f21b3cff_639x794.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:false,&quot;imageSize&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;height&quot;:819,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:728,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;captionedImage&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mZ-P!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd8f6dad4-eb94-4b40-bfac-bdc9f21b3cff_639x794.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mZ-P!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd8f6dad4-eb94-4b40-bfac-bdc9f21b3cff_639x794.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mZ-P!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd8f6dad4-eb94-4b40-bfac-bdc9f21b3cff_639x794.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mZ-P!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd8f6dad4-eb94-4b40-bfac-bdc9f21b3cff_639x794.png 1456w" sizes="100vw"></picture></div></a></figure></div><p>In the top part of the sample we do see some transparency, with the 5mm x 5mm grid showing through. The visual quality of the chicken breast takes on a gummy-bear like quality. Kinda makes me wanna chew it if it wouldn't give me Salmonella.</p><div><figure><a target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rS2G!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F157f7e6f-4675-4721-a001-ec96c245b120_4032x3024.jpeg" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rS2G!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F157f7e6f-4675-4721-a001-ec96c245b120_4032x3024.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rS2G!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F157f7e6f-4675-4721-a001-ec96c245b120_4032x3024.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rS2G!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F157f7e6f-4675-4721-a001-ec96c245b120_4032x3024.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rS2G!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F157f7e6f-4675-4721-a001-ec96c245b120_4032x3024.jpeg 1456w" sizes="100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rS2G!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F157f7e6f-4675-4721-a001-ec96c245b120_4032x3024.jpeg" width="728" height="409.5" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/157f7e6f-4675-4721-a001-ec96c245b120_4032x3024.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:false,&quot;imageSize&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;height&quot;:819,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:728,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;captionedImage&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rS2G!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F157f7e6f-4675-4721-a001-ec96c245b120_4032x3024.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rS2G!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F157f7e6f-4675-4721-a001-ec96c245b120_4032x3024.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rS2G!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F157f7e6f-4675-4721-a001-ec96c245b120_4032x3024.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rS2G!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F157f7e6f-4675-4721-a001-ec96c245b120_4032x3024.jpeg 1456w" sizes="100vw"></picture></div></a></figure></div><p>I don't wanna get copyrighted by Doritos so here is a cartoon of where you can find tartrazine in the wild.</p><div><figure><a target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Sqkw!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc157d29a-3e59-4320-8fc4-7ceaba5f1c65_1151x914.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Sqkw!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc157d29a-3e59-4320-8fc4-7ceaba5f1c65_1151x914.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Sqkw!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc157d29a-3e59-4320-8fc4-7ceaba5f1c65_1151x914.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Sqkw!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc157d29a-3e59-4320-8fc4-7ceaba5f1c65_1151x914.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Sqkw!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc157d29a-3e59-4320-8fc4-7ceaba5f1c65_1151x914.png 1456w" sizes="100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Sqkw!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc157d29a-3e59-4320-8fc4-7ceaba5f1c65_1151x914.png" width="728" height="409.5" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/c157d29a-3e59-4320-8fc4-7ceaba5f1c65_1151x914.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:false,&quot;imageSize&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;height&quot;:819,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:728,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;captionedImage&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Sqkw!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc157d29a-3e59-4320-8fc4-7ceaba5f1c65_1151x914.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Sqkw!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc157d29a-3e59-4320-8fc4-7ceaba5f1c65_1151x914.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Sqkw!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc157d29a-3e59-4320-8fc4-7ceaba5f1c65_1151x914.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Sqkw!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc157d29a-3e59-4320-8fc4-7ceaba5f1c65_1151x914.png 1456w" sizes="100vw" loading="lazy"></picture></div></a></figure></div><p>How does this work? </p><p>The current model we have is that the absorbance properties of the tartrazine also shift the refractive index of water. By pushing the refractive index of water to that of protein and lipid solution, we make the object more transparent. I’ll explain this in great detail later. </p><p>Tartrazine was from APC Pure. It was &gt;80% dye content, which means some uncertainty over what the true molar concentration will be. I then prepared three concentrations of tartrazine at these molar concentrations, one of which was just a 0 concentration as a control.</p><ul><li><p>Tartrazine: 0 g, Tap water: 20 g, w/w: 0%, Molality (mol/kg water): 0, Tartrazine (mmol): 0, Molarity (approx.): 0 M (control)</p></li><li><p>Tartrazine: 2 g, Tap water: 18 g, w/w: 10%, Molality (mol/kg water): 0.21, Tartrazine (mmol): 3.7, Molarity (approx.): ~0.19 M</p></li><li><p>Tartrazine: 6 g, Tap water: 14 g, w/w: 30%, Molality (mol/kg water): 0.80, Tartrazine (mmol): 11.2, Molarity (approx.): ~0.56 M</p></li></ul><p>Tartrazine has M = 534.4 g/mol. Moles use the nominal mass (the powder is &gt;80% dye, so true values are up to ~15% lower). Molarity assumes a final solution volume of ~20 mL.</p><p>This is what the tartrazine looked like. It doesn't have an odour, and it seems to be considered food safe by the FDA, so I didn't bother wearing gloves for this bit. Here is a picture of the tartrazine and the specs.</p><div><figure><a target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!LDMw!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0841d52d-2c4c-4dbb-8c7d-3825eacf6636_1887x1017.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!LDMw!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0841d52d-2c4c-4dbb-8c7d-3825eacf6636_1887x1017.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!LDMw!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0841d52d-2c4c-4dbb-8c7d-3825eacf6636_1887x1017.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!LDMw!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0841d52d-2c4c-4dbb-8c7d-3825eacf6636_1887x1017.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!LDMw!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0841d52d-2c4c-4dbb-8c7d-3825eacf6636_1887x1017.png 1456w" sizes="100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!LDMw!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%