e_2025x1350.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:false,&quot;imageSize&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;height&quot;:819,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:728,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;captionedImage&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!0yqk!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F680a059b-9189-4cb2-a25e-7af403e9bb9e_2025x1350.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!0yqk!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F680a059b-9189-4cb2-a25e-7af403e9bb9e_2025x1350.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!0yqk!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F680a059b-9189-4cb2-a25e-7af403e9bb9e_2025x1350.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!0yqk!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F680a059b-9189-4cb2-a25e-7af403e9bb9e_2025x1350.png 1456w" sizes="100vw" loading="lazy"></picture></div></a></figure></div><p>I threw these pieces out and then tried again with the method below.</p><p>And then I tried again with the same procedure, with the aim of soaking it for 12 hours at room temperature. Given the issues with the highest concentration (~0.56 M), I only tried the water control and the middle concentration (~0.19 M). But this time I put the chicken in test tubes and covered it, given that I was gonna leave it out for 12 hours at room temperature. I wanted to mitigate the food safety risk.</p><div><f