<p dir="auto">Blogging my personal ramblings at <a href="https://frenck.dev/" rel="nofollow">frenck.dev</a></p></div></div></li><li data-timeline-event-id="CE_lADOAbAFe88AAAABXwwfDM8AAAAHy1F9aA" data-highlighted-event="false" data-testid="timeline-row-border-CE_lADOAbAFe88AAAABXwwfDM8AAAAHy1F9aA" data-wrapper-timeline-id="CE_lADOAbAFe88AAAABXwwfDM8AAAAHy1F9aA"></li><li data-wrapper-timeline-id="IC_kwDOAbAFe88AAAABcvIL5g"><div data-testid="timeline-row-border-IC_kwDOAbAFe88AAAABcvIL5g" data-timeline-event-id="IC_kwDOAbAFe88AAAABcvIL5g" data-highlighted-event="false"><div id="issuecomment-6223432678" data-testid="comment-header"><h3>Viss<!-- --> <!-- -->commented<!-- --> <relative-time data-component="RelativeTime">on<!-- --> <!-- -->Oct 16, 2026<!-- --> </relative-time></h3><p><a data-component="Link" href="https://github.com/Viss" aria-label="@Viss's profile"><img data-component="Avatar" alt="@Viss" width="24" height="24" src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1756255?u=7ed4ec158e6547add67647f555631a64471c865a&amp;v=4&amp;size=48" data-testid="github-avatar"></a></p></div><div><div data-testid="markdown-body" data-team-hovercards-enabled="true" data-turbolinks="false"><p dir="auto">I run Phobos Group, and I travel all over the world giving presentations about security.<br>
I am very well acquainted with HIBP, and have met troy in the past.<br>
I helped deploy 1password at twitter when I was their sole red-team staff member in 2011.</p>
<p dir="auto">I am still not happy that home assistant, without my opt-in, without my permission, scanned my HA installation and send stuff up the line to HIBP.</p>
<p dir="auto">This should be an opt-in feature, and not something that 'just happens'.<br>
As a red teamer, I can give you a list as long as my arm about how I could abuse this to loot credentials from every HA install on the planet.</p></div><div role="toolbar" aria-label="Reactions"><p><span id="_R_1ml4vbnnd685H2_">Reacted by <!-- -->Daniel W. Crompton</span></p></div></div></div></li><li data-wrapper-timeline-id="IC_kwDOAbAFe88AAAABcvLpAA"><div data-testid="timeline-row-border-IC_kwDOAbAFe88AAAABcvLpAA" data-timeline-event-id="IC_kwDOAbAFe88AAAABcvLpAA" data-highlighted-event="false"><div id="issuecomment-6223489280" data-testid="comment-header"><h3>Viss<!-- --> <!-- -->commented<!-- --> <relative-time data-component="RelativeTime">on<!-- --> <!-- -->Oct 16, 2026<!-- --> </relative-time></h3><p><a data-component="Link" href="https://github.com/Viss" aria-label="@Viss's profile"><img data-component="Avatar" alt="@Viss" width="24" height="24" src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1756255?u=7ed4ec158e6547add67647f555631a64471c865a&amp;v=4&amp;size=48" data-testid="github-avatar"></a></p></div><div><div data-testid="markdown-body" data-team-hovercards-enabled="true" data-turbolinks="false"><p dir="auto">this issue is not closed until I am satisfied that HA is not taking things off my system without my permission and sending them to a 3rd party</p></div><div role="toolbar" aria-label="Reactions"><p><span id="_R_1ml5vbnnd685H2_">Reacted by <!-- -->Daniel W. Crompton</span></p></div></div></div></li><li data-wrapper-timeline-id="IC_kwDOAbAFe88AAAABcvP4bg"><div data-testid="timeline-row-border-IC_kwDOAbAFe88AAAABcvP4bg" data-timeline-event-id="IC_kwDOAbAFe88AAAABcvP4bg" data-highlighted-event="false"><div id="issuecomment-6223558766" data-testid="comment-header"><h3>frenck<!-- --> <!-- -->commented<!-- --> <relative-time data-component="RelativeTime">on<!-- --> <!-- -->Oct 16, 2026<!-- --> </relative-time></h3><p><a data-component="Link" href="https://github.com/frenck" aria-label="@frenck's profile"><img data-component="Avatar" alt="@frenck" width="24" height="24" src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/195327?u=c0f88e376380f7a811559aa54d5096a66f6d3488&amp;v=4&amp;size=48" data-testid="github-avatar"></a></p></div><div><div data-testid="markdown-body" data-team-hovercards-enabled="true" data-turbolinks="false"><p dir="auto">This issue is closed as won't fix. Sorry.</p>
<p dir="auto">../Frenck</p></div><div role="toolbar" aria-label="Reactions"><p><span id="_R_1ml6vbnnd685H2_">Reacted by <!-- -->Latte macchiato</span></p><p><span id="_R_2ml6vbnnd685H2_">Reacted by <!-- -->Ryan Carter, Ben Lee, Ciarán Ainsworth, Daniel W. Crompton, xor eax,eax and Jamie Bliss</span></p></div></div></div></li><li data-wrapper-timeline-id="IC_kwDOAbAFe88AAAABcvf2tA"><div data-testid="timeline-row-border-IC_kwDOAbAFe88AAAABcvf2tA" data-timeline-event-id="IC_kwDOAbAFe88AAAABcvf2tA" data-highlighted-event="false"><div id="issuecomment-6223820468" data-testid="comment-header"><h3>0x00string<!-- --> <!-- -->commented<!-- --> <relative-time data-component="RelativeTime">on<!-- --> <!-- -->Oct 16, 2026<!-- --> </relative-time></h3><p><a data-component="Link" href="https://github.com/0x00string" aria-label="@0x00string's profile"><img data-component="Avatar" alt="@0x00string" width="24" height="24" src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7436534?u=9da85721bdc11595aa2ec831a5062cc422b7635d&amp;v=4&amp;size=48" data-testid="github-avatar"></a></p></div><div><div data-testid="markdown-body" data-team-hovercards-enabled="true" data-turbolinks="false"><p dir="auto">Hi, long time HA user here. Please re-open this issue and address the question of how to disable this. If a method to disable it is not currently implemented, please consider implementing this rather than insisting the userbase accept this and take your word on it. This response feels extremely dismissive and as a user of this platform I feel secondhand offended by it as I share the exact same concerns as OP and do not believe the response here adequately addressed the concerns.</p>
<p dir="auto">If there is no interest in addressing this reasonably, please let us know so we can uninstall and fork.</p></div><div role="toolbar" aria-label="Reactions"><p><span id="_R_1ml7vbnnd685H2_">Reacted by <!-- -->Daniel W. Crompton</span></p><p><span id="_R_6ml7vbnnd685H2_">Reacted by <!-- -->Justin Myers</span></p></div></div></div></li><li data-wrapper-timeline-id="IC_kwDOAbAFe88AAAABcvimbQ"><div data-testid="timeline-row-border-IC_kwDOAbAFe88AAAABcvimbQ" data-timeline-event-id="IC_kwDOAbAFe88AAAABcvimbQ" data-highlighted-event="false"><div id="issuecomment-6223865453" data-testid="comment-header"><h3>frenck<!-- --> <!-- -->commented<!-- --> <relative-time data-component="RelativeTime">on<!-- --> <!-- -->Oct 16, 2026<!-- --> </relative-time></h3><p><a data-component="Link" href="https://github.com/frenck" aria-label="@frenck's profile"><img data-component="Avatar" alt="@frenck" width="24" height="24" src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/195327?u=c0f88e376380f7a811559aa54d5096a66f6d3488&amp;v=4&amp;size=48" data-testid="github-avatar"></a></p></div><div data-testid="markdown-body" data-team-hovercards-enabled="true" data-turbolinks="false"><blockquote>
<p dir="auto">please let us know so we can uninstall and fork</p>
</blockquote>
<p dir="auto">Sorry, these are not statements we can work with. Doing such threats and trying to intimidate it not going to bring you anywhere. If you want to do a feature request, that is fine, we have places for that.</p>
<p dir="auto">This report is on our documentation. There is no amount of documentation I can adjust to adjust this or address this. Thus closed as won't fix.</p>
<p dir="auto">If this is all reason for you to uninstall and fork... 🤷 So be it, it is open source after all.</p>
