            <title><![CDATA[Llama.cpp on a jailbroken PS5: run any GGUF model natively on the console (347 pts)]]></title>
            <link>https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM</link>
            <guid>50122431</guid>
            <pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:32:35 GMT</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM">https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM</a>, See on <a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50122431">Hacker News</a></p>
<div id="readability-page-1" class="page"><div data-hpc="true" containertiming="hpc"><article itemprop="text"><p dir="auto">
  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM/blob/main/ps5/app/sce_sys/icon0.png"><img src="https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM/raw/main/ps5/app/sce_sys/icon0.png" width="128" alt="PS5LM"></a>
</p>

<p dir="auto">
  <b>Your PS5 runs the language model. Every device on your network uses it.</b><br>
  llama.cpp on the console's GPU, with OpenAI and Anthropic APIs and a screen made for the TV.
</p>
<p dir="auto">
  <b><a href="https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM/releases/latest">Get the app</a></b> ·
  <a href="https://ps5lm.cobanov.dev/" rel="nofollow">Website</a> ·
  <a href="#try-it">Get started</a> ·
  <a href="https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM/issues">Issues</a>
</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto"><strong>New: decision models, powered by <a href="https://ollaya.dev/" rel="nofollow">Ollaya</a>.</strong> PS5LM now runs Jev-like
decision models (d1, Clef, OpenJev and more) on the GPU and answers the same <code>/v1/systemone</code>
API as Ollaya: typed decisions with calibrated probabilities, in a fraction of a second.</p>
</blockquote>
<p dir="auto">PS5LM is for anyone with a jailbroken PS5 who wants a private model server at home. It loads a GGUF
model onto the console's GPU and serves it to your laptop, your phone and your coding tools. It needs
no PC while it runs, no cloud and no account.</p>
<p dir="auto">
  <a href="https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM/blob/main/docs/media/ps5lm-home.mp4"><img src="https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM/raw/main/docs/media/ps5lm-home.gif" width="720" alt="Qwen 3.5 9B generating on a PS5, with the requests streaming across the TV" data-animated-image=""></a><br>
  <sub>Qwen 3.5 9B answering requests from a laptop on a PS5 Slim. Click for the video.</sub>
</p>
<p dir="auto">
  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM/blob/main/docs/media/app/home.jpg"><img src="https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM/raw/main/docs/media/app/home.jpg" width="49%" alt="Home: the model, its speed and the live requests"></a>
  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM/blob/main/docs/media/app/models.jpg"><img src="https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM/raw/main/docs/media/app/models.jpg" width="49%" alt="Models: the ones suggested for the PS5"></a>
  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM/blob/main/docs/media/app/home-decision.jpg"><img src="https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM/raw/main/docs/media/app/home-decision.jpg" width="49%" alt="Home with a decision model"></a>
  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM/blob/main/docs/media/app/console.jpg"><img src="https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM/raw/main/docs/media/app/console.jpg" width="49%" alt="Console: temperature, power and load over time"></a>
  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM/blob/main/docs/media/app/api.jpg"><img src="https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM/raw/main/docs/media/app/api.jpg" width="49%" alt="API: the endpoints and an example"></a>
  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM/blob/main/docs/media/app/settings.jpg"><img src="https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM/raw/main/docs/media/app/settings.jpg" width="49%" alt="Settings: a list of choices under the row"></a>
  <br><sub>Home, Models, Console, API and Settings on the TV.</sub>
</p>
<p dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" dir="auto">A model server under your TV</h2><a id="user-content-a-model-server-under-your-tv" aria-label="Permalink: A model server under your TV" href="#a-model-server-under-your-tv"></a></p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><strong>It runs on the GPU.</strong> llama.cpp's Vulkan backend on the console's RDNA 2 GPU, with 11.4 GB of the
shared memory for the model and its context. Every architecture and quantization llama.cpp knows
comes along.</li>
<li><strong>It answers your network.</strong> OpenAI's <code>/v1/chat/completions</code>, Anthropic's <code>/v1/messages</code> (Claude Code
works against it) and a chat page in any browser. Point a client at <code>http://&lt;console&gt;:8081</code> and use
any model name: the loaded one answers.</li>
<li><strong>It decides, too.</strong> Load a decision model and the console answers TypeSafe's <code>/v1/systemone</code>:
choice, score and yes-or-no questions about text and images, the API Ollaya serves on a PC.</li>
<li><strong>It shows its work.</strong> Every request streams across the TV as a chat: which device asked, what it
asked, and the reply as it is written. Square sends a demo and Triangle opens a keyboard, so the
console can be tried from the couch.</li>
<li><strong>It watches the console.</strong> A Console page charts temperature, power, GPU and CPU load over the
last two minutes or the last hour, beside a table of every reading.</li>
<li><strong>It picks what fits.</strong> The planner reads each GGUF and gives it the longest context and best cache
that fit the memory free. A Suggested list holds models measured on the console, and the app
downloads from Hugging Face by itself, to internal storage, the M.2 drive or a USB drive.</li>
<li><strong>It reads images.</strong> Models with an image projector (Gemma 4, MiniCPM-V, d1) take pictures in chat
and in decisions.</li>
</ul>
<markdown-accessiblity-table><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Model</th>
<th>Size</th>
<th>On a PS5 Slim</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Qwen 3.5 0.8B, Q4_K_M</td>
<td>0.5 GB</td>
<td>207 tokens a second</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Qwen 3.5 9B, Q4_K_M</td>
<td>5.3 GB</td>
<td>55 tokens a second</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Qwen 3.8 27B, UD-Q2_K_XL</td>
<td>9.2 GB</td>
<td>about 20 tokens a second, 64k context</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>d1 Omni 600M, a decision model</td>
<td>1.1 GB</td>
<td>3 questions in 0.3 s; a 720p image and 7 questions in 2.9 s</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
<p dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" dir="auto">Decision models, powered by Ollaya</h2><a id="user-content-decision-models-powered-by-ollaya" aria-label="Permalink: Decision models, powered by Ollaya" href="#decision-models-powered-by-ollaya"></a></p>
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://github.com/ollaya-dev/ollaya">Ollaya</a> runs open decision models on a PC the way Ollama runs
language models. PS5LM brings the same idea to the console: a decision model reads a state and
answers typed questions in one forward pass, with no text generated.</p>
<div dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="curl http://<console>:8081/v1/systemone -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{
  &quot;state&quot;: &quot;I was charged twice this month. Refund me or I cancel.&quot;,
  &quot;questions&quot;: {
    &quot;intent&quot;: {&quot;type&quot;: &quot;choice&quot;, &quot;instructions&quot;: &quot;What does the customer want?&quot;,
               &quot;criteria&quot;: {&quot;refund&quot;: null, &quot;information&quot;: null, &quot;cancel&quot;: null}},
    &quot;angry&quot;:  {&quot;type&quot;: &quot;noul&quot;, &quot;instructions&quot;: &quot;Is the customer angry?&quot;}
  }
}'"><pre>curl http://<span>&lt;</span>console<span>&gt;</span>:8081/v1/systemone -H <span><span>'</span>Content-Type: application/json<span>'</span></span> -d <span><span>'</span>{</span>
<span>  "state": "I was charged twice this month. Refund me or I cancel.",</span>
<span>  "questions": {</span>
<span>    "intent": {"type": "choice", "instructions": "What does the customer want?",</span>
<span>               "criteria": {"refund": null, "information": null, "cancel": null}},</span>
<span>    "angry":  {"type": "noul", "instructions": "Is the customer angry?"}</span>
<span>  }</span>
<span>}<span>'</span></span></pre></div>
<p dir="auto">The Suggested list has d1 Omni 600M, d1 3B and Clef Flash. Any GGUF that carries llama.cpp's
decision metadata loads the same way, and the app labels it a decision model.</p>
<p dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" dir="auto">Try it</h2><a id="user-content-try-it" aria-label="Permalink: Try it" href="#try-it"></a></p>
<p dir="auto">You need a PS5 on firmware 7.00 to 13.60, jailbroken, with these payloads loaded:</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Payload</th>
<th>For</th>
<th></th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><a href="https://github.com/EchoStretch/kstuff-lite">kstuff-lite</a></td>
<td>the kernel patches homebrew runs on</td>
<td>required</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><a href="https://github.com/etaHEN/etaHEN">etaHEN</a></td>
<td>homebrew support</td>
<td>required</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><a href="https://github.com/drakmor/ShadowMountPlus">ShadowMountPlus</a></td>
<td>puts PS5LM on the home screen from <code>/data/homebrew</code></td>
<td>required</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><a href="https://github.com/ps5-payload-dev/elfldr">elfldr</a> (port 9021)</td>
<td>temperature, power and real free space, through ps5-exporter</td>
<td>recommended</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><a href="https://github.com/ps5-payload-dev/ftpsrv">ftpsrv</a> (port 2121)</td>
<td>installing the app, copying models from a PC</td>
<td>recommended</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
<ol dir="auto">
<li>Download <code>ps5lm-app-vX.Y.Z.zip</code> from the <a href="https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM/releases/latest">latest release</a> and unzip it.</li>
<li>Copy the <code>PPSA99575</code> folder to <code>/data/homebrew</code> over FTP. ShadowMountPlus adds <strong>PS5LM</strong> to the
home screen.</li>
<li>Open PS5LM, go to <strong>Models &gt; Suggested</strong> and get a model. Or copy a <code>.gguf</code> to
<code>/data/PS5LM/models</code>, or to <code>PS5LM/models</code> on a USB drive.</li>
<li>Load it. Once Home says Ready, open <code>http://&lt;console&gt;:8081</code> in a browser, or point your OpenAI or
Anthropic client at it.</li>
</ol>
<p dir="auto">To update, copy the new folder over the old one. Settings, models and downloads stay in
<code>/data/PS5LM</code>. Using it from coding tools (opencode, Codex, Claude Code) is in
<a href="https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM/blob/main/docs/CLI.md">docs/CLI.md</a>.</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Where</th>
<th>Button</th>
<th>Does</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Everywhere</td>
<td>L1 / R1</td>
<td>Home, Models, API, Console, Settings</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Home</td>
<td>Cross</td>
<td>change the model</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Home</td>
<td>Square / Triangle</td>
<td>send a demo request / type a message</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Models</td>
<td>D-pad, Cross</td>
<td>choose a section and a model; load, unload or download it</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Models, Search</td>
<td>L2 / R2, Square</td>
<td>change the search; check whether a file fits</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Models, Downloads</td>
<td>Cross, Square</td>
<td>pause or resume; cancel (press twice) or clear</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Console</td>
<td>L2 / R2</td>
<td>the last two minutes / the last hour</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Settings</td>
<td>D-pad, Cross</td>
<td>choose a category and a row; flip it, or pick from its list</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Settings, Diagnostics</td>
<td>Square, Triangle</td>
<td>app or server log; errors only</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
<p dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" dir="auto">Want to tinker?</h2><a id="user-content-want-to-tinker" aria-label="Permalink: Want to tinker?" href="#want-to-tinker"></a></p>
<p dir="auto">C++ on <a href="https://github.com/blackbearreloaded/ps5-homebrew-ui">ps5-homebrew-ui</a>, llama.cpp with
ggml-vulkan on <a href="https://github.com/mihawk-99/PS5_Vulkan">PS5_Vulkan</a>'s RADV, built on Linux.</p>
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM/blob/main/docs/BUILDING.md">Building</a> · <a href="https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM/blob/main/docs/CONSOLE.md">Console notes</a> · <a href="https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM/blob/main/docs/PORTING.md">Porting</a> ·
<a href="https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM/blob/main/docs/RESEARCH.md">Research</a> · <a href="https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM/blob/main/docs/MODELS.md">Models that fit</a> · <a href="https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM/blob/main/docs/ROADMAP.md">Roadmap</a> ·
<a href="https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md">Changelog</a> · <a href="https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM/blob/main/docs/PAYLOAD.md">The original payload</a></p>
<p dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" dir="auto">Thanks</h2><a id="user-content-thanks" aria-label="Permalink: Thanks" href="#thanks"></a></p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><a href="https://github.com/abhi245y">abhi245y</a>, who built the native GPU app this one grew from (PS5LM Plus).</li>
<li><a href="https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp">llama.cpp and ggml</a>, which do the actual work.</li>
<li><a href="https://github.com/mihawk-99">Mihawk-99</a> for PS5_Vulkan and RADV on the PS5, and
<a href="https://github.com/premohq/PS5CEMU-HAR">PS5CEMU-HAR</a> for the driver patches in <code>patches/mesa</code>.</li>
<li><a href="https://github.com/blackbearreloaded">BlackBearReloaded</a> for ps5-homebrew-ui, ps5-opengl and
ps5-homebrew-dev-protocol, and <a href="https://github.com/ps5-payload-dev">John Törnblom</a> for the SDK.</li>
<li><a href="https://github.com/Marice/ps5-exporter">Marice</a> for ps5-exporter, which the app carries.</li>
<li><a href="https://github.com/sharanda/manrope">Manrope</a> (OFL) for the type, and
<a href="https://github.com/cobanov/pocketvibe">PocketVibe</a> for the interface sounds.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<p dir="auto">GPL-3.0-or-later, see <a href="https://github.com/cobanov/PS5LM/blob/main/LICENSE">LICENSE</a>. llama.cpp keeps its MIT licence, Manrope its OFL. No Sony
SDK files, keys, firmware or model weights are in this repository.</p>
<p dir="auto">PS5LM is not affiliated with Sony Interactive Entertainment. "PlayStation" and "PS5" are trademarks
of Sony Interactive Entertainment.</p>
</article></div></div>]]></description>
